<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Indian princely states</p><h1 class="st-title">Koch Kingdom</h1><p class="st-meta">1515 CE – 1581 CE (approx.) · capital Cooch Behar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The Koch kingdom of Biswa Singha and Nara Narayan, which briefly dominated north-east India in the 16th century before splitting into Koch Bihar and Koch Hajo.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/bengal-sultanate">Bengal Sultanate</a> destroyed the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kamata-kingdom">Kamata Kingdom</a> around 1498, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biswa-singha">Biswa Singha</a>, a leader of the Koch people, united the local chiefs and founded a new state around 1515, centred on the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cooch-behar-state">Cooch Behar</a> area. He adopted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hinduism">Hindu</a> kingship and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> rituals.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara-narayan">Nara Narayan</a> (r. 1540–1587) and his brother and general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chilarai">Chilarai</a>, the Koch defeated the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/ahom-kingdom">Ahom kingdom</a> and, according to later chronicles, forced tribute from the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kachari-kingdom">Kachari kingdom</a>, Jaintia, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-manipur">Manipur</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripura">Tripura</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara">Nara</a> Narayan rebuilt the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kamakhya-temple">Kamakhya</a> temple and patronised the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vaishnavism">Vaishnava</a> saint <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/srimanta-sankardev">Sankardev</a> and Assamese and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sanskrit">Sanskrit</a> literature.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 1581 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nara-narayan">Nara Narayan</a> divided the kingdom with his nephew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/raghudev-narayan">Raghudev</a>, creating <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/cooch-behar-state">Koch Bihar</a> in the west and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/koch-hajo">Koch Hajo</a> in the east. Koch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bihar">Bihar</a> continued as Cooch Behar State; Koch <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hajo">Hajo</a> was later absorbed by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mughal-empire">Mughals</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ahom-people">Ahoms</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="kingdom, 1515 CE – 1581 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 72 V40 L36 54 L50 28 L64 54 L78 40 V72 Z"/><path d="M22 80 H78"/><circle cx="50" cy="24" r="3"/><circle cx="22" cy="36" r="2.5"/><circle cx="78" cy="36" r="2.5"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">kingdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Indian princely states</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:89.85%;width:1.31%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1515 CE – 1581 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Cooch Behar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Biswa Singha, Nara Narayan</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Hinduism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Kamtapuri, Assamese</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/india">India</a>, <a href="/countries/bangladesh">Bangladesh</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kamata-Koch Kingdom</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1548&amp;focus=koch-kingdom" aria-label="Koch Kingdom on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="7040 1211 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Koch Kingdom lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M7360 1467L7416 1470M7360 1467L7350 1471"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M7416 1470h0M7350 1471h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M7360 1467h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M7360 1467h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Cooch Behar. <a href="/atlas?year=1548&amp;focus=koch-kingdom">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
